WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.102 line:0%
-What is this?

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:07.607 line:0%
-What does it look like, dummy?

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:10.109 line:0%
It's a bridge of spies.

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:12.245 line:0%
Go away.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:14.447 line:0%
We're spying.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:22.855
-I want to test you a little
bit, you know, see what you got.

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.190
-You got it. Bring it on.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.459
-So I was thinking maybe
you could perform a few scenes

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.928
from "Bridge of Spies"
for us right now.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.630
How does that sound?
-Challenging but fun.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.064
Let's do it.
-That'd be fun?

00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:34.534
Now, here's the catch --
the scenes are not from

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.103
the actual movie.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:40.506
They were all written by
elementary school kids.

00:00:40.506 --> 00:00:42.442
We gave them no direction,

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:45.678
just the title
"Bridge of Spies."

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.847
Alright, here we go.
It's time for "Kid Theater."

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:48.981
Here we go.

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:51.116
-♪ Kid Theater ♪

00:00:51.116 --> 00:00:54.154
♪ Kid Theater ♪

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.457
-Alright.
-Alright.

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:59.392
This first one,
here's your script.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:00.993
-Thank you very much.
-No problem.

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:03.696
This one is from Chris.
He's 8 years old.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:06.532
You'll be playing
the role of spy.

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:07.867
-Yes.
-And I will be playing

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.136
the role of man.
-Okay.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.938
-Higgins will read the scene
descriptions for us.

00:01:12.938 --> 00:01:14.507
Higgins, set the scene, please.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:17.076 line:0%
-There was once a bridge
that was full of spies.

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:20.646 line:0%
A man walked up to it.

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:23.549 line:0%
-What is this?

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:28.087 line:0%
-What does it look like, dummy?

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.689 line:0%
It's a bridge of spies.

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:32.792 line:0%
Go away.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:35.495 line:0%
We're spying.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:40.232 line:0%
-Can I be a spy?

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:42.168 line:0%
-No.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:45.271 line:0%
This bridge is too full of spies
already.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:48.241 line:0%
There's not room for any more.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:51.778 line:0%
-Who are you spying on?

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:54.714 line:0%
-Each other.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.649 line:0%
-How?

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:59.953 line:0%
-You sure ask a lot of questions
for someone who is not a spy.

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.754 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.757 line:0%
-Maybe I<i> am</i> a spy.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.560 line:0%
-Are you?

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.630 line:0%
-No.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.399 line:0%
-Are you sure?

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:15.001 line:0%
-No.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:18.303 line:0%
-The man rips off his mask.

00:02:18.303 --> 00:02:19.839 line:0%
-You are a spy!

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:22.108 line:0%
-Exactly!
And you fell for my trick.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.611 line:0%
Therefore you are
no longer a spy.

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.045 line:0%
Hahahahaha!

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:28.781 line:0%
-Hahahahaha!

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:32.885 line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:34.754 line:0%
-What are you laughing at?

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:38.925 line:0%
-Nothing. I just wanted to
keep acting like a spy.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.693 line:0%
-And scene.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.996 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.731 --> 00:02:47.233
-That is a very --
-That is a nice one.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:49.669
-That is a nice one.
-You're keeping that one?

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:52.405
-That deserves a second look.
I think it really does.

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:54.173
-This is the second one here
for you.

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:56.542
-Let's see what this one is.
-This is sent in by Jack.

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:58.077
He is 7 years old.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.712
For this one, I'll play Joe,

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.647
and you'll play
the role of Margaret.

00:03:01.647 --> 00:03:05.150
-Let me adjust my --
Alright, I am now Margaret.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.652
-You are Margaret and I am Joe.

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:08.988
Okay, Higgins, will you set
the scene for us, please?

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:11.624 line:0%
-Margaret walks up to Joe
on the sidewalk.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.993 line:0%
-Hi, Joe!

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.995 line:0%
-Hey, Tim! I mean Margaret!

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:18.264 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.600 line:0%
-Joe, how do you get me
and your brother mixed up?

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.902 line:0%
We've been going out
for eight years!

00:03:23.902 --> 00:03:27.440 line:0%
-Sorry, you kind of look alike.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.443 line:0%
-Anyway, did you hear about
the new bridge?

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:31.777 line:0%
-What bridge?

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:34.914 line:0%
-You know! The bridge of spies!

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:37.750 line:0%
-No! What the heck is that?

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.352 line:0%
-Well, I'll tell you...

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.853 line:0%
-Wait!

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.355 line:0%
-What?

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.456 line:0%
-Okay, never mind.

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:45.191 line:0%
I thought you were Tim
for a second.

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:47.360 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.296 line:0%
Tell me about the new bridge.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:53.066 line:0%
-Well, they're gonna build
this new bridge

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.101 line:0%
somewhere in China or something,

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:57.837 line:0%
and they're gonna call it
the bridge of spies

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.638 line:0%
'cause they are finding spies

00:03:59.638 --> 00:04:02.175 line:0%
and taping them together
to make a bridge.

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.676 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.676 --> 00:04:08.047 line:0%
-Wow! That's gonna take
like a hundred years!

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:10.249 line:0%
-Yeah!
They didn't have enough wood,

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:12.151 line:0%
so they're gonna use spies.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.820 line:0%
-What do the spies think of it?

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:18.124 line:0%
-I don't know the spies, Joe.

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:20.627 line:0%
-Sorry for asking, Tim.

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:23.429 line:0%
-I'm not your brother,
I'm Margaret!

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:25.598 line:0%
-Want to get dinner?
-Yes. Cake, please.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.233 line:0%
-And scene.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:29.568 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:31.603
Think about it. Think about it.

00:04:31.603 --> 00:04:33.605
I'll take that one.
-You want that one?

00:04:33.605 --> 00:04:34.807
Take another look at that.

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.142
-I'll take another look
at that one.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:37.376
-A little polish on that,
a little rewrite.

00:04:37.376 --> 00:04:38.611
-And I'll get it back to you.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:41.314
This last one here,
this is the last one,

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:42.448
sent in by Luke.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.049
He's 7 years old.

00:04:44.049 --> 00:04:45.184
Thank you for sending these in.

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:48.087
Tom, you'll be playing Spy #1.
-Spy #1.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.289
-And I'll be playing Spy #2.

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:53.059
-Alright. Spy #1.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.994
-Higgins, set the scene, please.

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:57.063 line:0%
-Two spies stand on a bridge.

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:59.632 line:0%
One of them has a pair
of binoculars.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:05.571 line:0%
-I can see bad guys
coming in the distance.

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.039 line:0%
-I wish I could see them too,

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:08.908 line:0%
but you're the one
with the binoculars.

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:11.711 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:24.690 line:0%
-It's not my fault
you forgot yours at home.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:28.494 line:0%
-It kinda is. You told me
we wouldn't need them today!

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:31.497 line:0%
-I was joking!

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:34.633 line:0%
We always need them.
We're spies!

00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:40.706 line:0%
-Obviously! But we're also
friends, so I trusted you!

00:05:40.706 --> 00:05:46.379 line:0%
-You should never trust a spy!

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:50.483 line:0%
-But what about trusting...
a friend spy?

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:53.118 line:0%
-Spy 1 and Spy 2
look at each other.

00:05:53.118 --> 00:05:55.488 line:0%
Spy 1 looks amazed.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.693 line:0%
-Wow.

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:04.096 line:0%
I never thought about it
like that before.

00:06:04.096 --> 00:06:12.338 line:0%
Maybe friendship is more
important than spying.

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:17.509 line:0%
-Exactly.

00:06:17.509 --> 00:06:22.114 line:0%
-Here.
You can have my binoculars.

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:23.215 line:0%
[ Audience "awws" ]

00:06:23.215 --> 00:06:26.485 line:0%
-Spy 1 hands over the binoculars
to Spy 2.

00:06:26.485 --> 00:06:28.921 line:0%
-Ha! You're such a loser.

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:30.756 line:0%
Rule number one of being a spy

00:06:30.756 --> 00:06:34.327 line:0%
